# Generated pages of the manual. None of them are committed: the showroom is the compiler's own
# output, the guarantee matrices are the report generators' output, and llms.txt is derived from the
# nav. A committed copy of any of them could only ever be a snapshot of some earlier run, which is
# exactly the staleness these pages exist to avoid. The Docs workflow produces the lot at publish
# time with `cmake --build <dir> --target docs-generate`; run that locally before previewing the
# site, or mkdocs --strict will fail on the nav entries with nothing behind them.
docs/showroom/
docs/reference/guarantees/parity-matrix.md
docs/reference/guarantees/malformed-input.md
docs/reference/guarantees/determinism.md
docs/development/convergence-scorecard.md
docs/llms.txt
docs/llms-full.txt
.venv-docs/

# Reference DSDL compiler checkouts for the differential parity lane (CI clones
# these; local runs may too). Provisioned, never committed.
.reference/

# Dafny scratch (verify emits nothing, but guard against stray build/backup output).
*.dfy.bak
spec/dafny/bin/
.claude/settings.json
compile_commands.json
